-- title:
--   Existence of a formal quotient datum for Drinfeld's half plane
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and with $(r)=(\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ and every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ with $Fr\,x\equiv x^r \pmod \pi$. Let $vdet:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) be a homomorphism with $vdet\,g=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\pi^n$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$. Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism and $\Gamma\le G$ a subgroup containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix and $vdet(\sigma z)=2$, and an element $w$ with $vdet(\sigma w)=1$; let $\Gamma'$ be a subgroup consisting exactly of those $x\in\Gamma$ with $vdet(\sigma x)$ even. Let $\rho:G\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be the homomorphism induced by $\sigma$, and assume the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ acts on the set of homothety classes of full $\mathcal O$-lattices in $K_0^2$ with finite vertex stabilisers and with finitely many orbits (a finite set of vertices meeting every orbit). Finally let $g_1=\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$. The conclusion is that the type $\mathtt{FormalQuotientDatum}$ for these data is nonempty: there exists a system of schemes $Y_n$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, with proper structure morphisms and with transition morphisms $Y_n\to Y_{n+1}$ exhibiting $Y_n$ as the base change of $Y_{n+1}$ along $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2}\to\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, together with maps $q_n$ sending, for each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ in $B$, a pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ for $\Omega$ (a family of $B$-submodules of the base-changed lattices with invertible quotients, monotone, homothety-equivariant and nondegenerate at every prime of $B$) to a $B$-point of $Y_n$, these maps being compatible with the structure morphism to $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, natural in $B$, compatible with the transition morphisms, and invariant under the twisted action of $\Gamma$ (Frobenius twist by $-vdet(\sigma\gamma)$ on the first component and pullback along $\sigma\gamma^{-1}$ of the Deligne datum), and satisfying the remaining conditions of the structure, which describe the geometric fibres, the unramified base change $Y_n^{nr}$ and the chart and comparison data, summarised here.
--
--   This is the existence of a formal model for the quotient of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane with unramified coefficients by a discrete cocompact group $\Gamma$, in the form required for the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation; $\Gamma'$ is the even part of $\Gamma$ and $g_1=\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ interchanges the two types of vertices. It is the input to the statements extracting closed points and chart morphisms from the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient.
